% Qatlib bibliography
% ===================
%
% Scope: foundational sources for Qatlib's concepts and all 302 paper
% directories under Qatlib/Papers (verified 2026-11-11). There are 7,267 Lean
% modules under Qatlib/: 380 Foundations, 3,719 Concepts, and 3,168 Papers.
% Paper-directory mappings use authoritative arXiv and publisher/DOI metadata.
% A published version may have a different title, author list, or year from
% its preprint; eprint and note fields preserve those connections.
% Topic coverage is not a claim that a complete paper, or every theorem in a
% cited work, has been formalized.
%
% Publication metadata was checked against publisher/DOI records, arXiv,
% and MathNet. Citekeys use ASCII author surnames and the publication year,
% with a short suffix when needed; author order follows the publication.
% Directory suffixes often reflect a preprint year rather than the year of
% the published version. Different volumes/editions have distinct keys.
% Abbreviated or ambiguous paper-family names alone are not enough to assign
% authors, titles, or identifiers; no speculative references are included.
%
% Entries are grouped by subject and sorted by citekey within each group.
% Related paths in comments are relative to Qatlib/ and are discovery aids.
% Mathematical background requested for the library is included even where
% no explicit source citation exists. Mathlib's bibliography remains separate;
% this file is self-contained and does not rely on crossref/string macros.
%
% Maintenance and doc-gen4 compatibility:
% - Cite an entry in Lean Markdown with [Author, *Title*][Citekey].
% - Keep the entire file ASCII, using LaTeX escapes for accented names.
% - Keep keys ASCII, starting with a letter; use letters, digits, :, -, or _.
% - Use literal braced field values, balanced braces, and explicit metadata.
% - Avoid string definitions, concatenation, preambles, and special comment
%   entries. In prose comments, avoid the at-sign: BibtexQuery scans for it
%   without recognizing percent comments.
% - Validate the entire input and the expected entry count. BibtexQuery's
%   file parser may otherwise silently return only a valid prefix.
% - Run doc-gen4's Bibtex.process and bibliography prepass too: parsing alone
%   does not check TeX/name conversion or reference-page formatting.
% - For article numbers, pages contains the publisher's article identifier.
%   Unpublished arXiv works have no invented journal, volume, or page range.
%
